  "problem": "Find a parametric equation of the osculating plane for the curve  $r(t)$ at the point where $t=\\pi $, given that\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,T(\\pi )=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨1,0,-1⟩,\\,N(\\pi )=⟨0,1,0⟩.\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively.",
